API-23 (public wrappers ignore their *Init result) reproducer, via a malloc
interposer that fails the N-th allocation.  Needs a NON-sanitized build
(ASan replaces malloc), so build libscotch with -fsanitize removed.

  gcc -O0 -g -shared -fPIC failmalloc.c -o failmalloc.so -ldl
  gcc -O0 -g -I<inc> map.c -o map -L<plainlib> -lscotch -lscotcherr -lz -lm -lpthread

  SCOTCH_FAIL_AT=3 LD_PRELOAD=./failmalloc.so LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<plainlib> ./map
   (call 3, 264 bytes, is SCOTCH_graphMapInit's part-array allocation)
   pristine : 'ERROR: SCOTCH_graphMapInit: out of memory' then Segmentation fault
              (rc=139): the ignored Init error let graphMapCompute run on an
              unallocated part array.
   patched  : 'ERROR: SCOTCH_graphMapInit: out of memory' then 'SCOTCH_graphMap ret=1'
              (rc=1): the wrapper returns the error instead of proceeding.
  (The graphCoarsen 1->2 return-code change is verified by source/doc reading.)
